  "next_id": 65,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -12,
        -34
      ],
      "id": 64,
      "text": "SPI1 of the Blue Pill (an STM32CubeIDE-style HAL project) sends words to a MAX7219, which scans an 8x8\nLED matrix 800 times a second: DIG0-DIG7 sink the rows, DP and A-G drive the columns. PA4 is the\nchip select (LOAD). The MAX7219 needs 5 V on VCC. Run (F5): a heart and a smiley take turns, brighter\neach time. Analyzer > Logic shows the SPI clock and data and the chip's DIG lanes (U2.DIG0...)."
    }
  ],
